Inheritance vs Polymorphism:
Inheritance allows child class to inherit properties from parent class for reusability and uses Inherits keyword.
Polymorphism allows same method to have different forms and behave differently in different classes and uses Overridable and Overrides.

Encapsulation is wrapping data and methods into a single unit and restricting direct access using Private modifier. It is important because it provides data security, controls access through properties, and makes code maintainable.

Constructors and Destructors:
Constructor is Sub New(). It is called automatically when object is created to initialize values.
Destructor is Sub Finalize(). It is called when object is destroyed to clean up resources like closing files.

