Part A: Input and Validation (6 marks) Design a form with textboxes for student name and marks in 4 course units (ICT, VisualBasic, Research methods and Cyber & computer law). Write validation code to ensure all fields are filled and marks are numeric values between 0-100, displaying appropriate error messages for invalid inputs.

Private Function ValidateInput() As Boolean
If txtStudentName.Text = "" Or txtICT.Text = "" Or txtVB.Text = "" Or txtResearch.Text = "" Or txtCyberLaw.Text = "" Then
MessageBox.Show("All fields must be filled!", "Validation Error", MessageBoxButtons.OK, MessageBoxIcon.Error)
Return False
End If
Dim marks() As TextBox = {txtICT, txtVB, txtResearch, txtCyberLaw}
For Each tb As TextBox In marks
If Not IsNumeric(tb.Text) Or Val(tb.Text) < 0 Or Val(tb.Text) > 100 Then
MessageBox.Show("Marks must be numeric between 0-100", "Invalid", MessageBoxButtons.OK, MessageBoxIcon.Warning)
Return False
End If
Next
Return True
End Function

Part B: Calculations and Grading (8 marks) Implement calculations for total marks, average percentage, and letter grades (A:90-100, B:80-89, C:70-79, D:60-69, F:below 60). Determine pass/fail status based on average ≥60%. Use proper variables and efficient logic.

Function GetGrade(mark As Double) As String
If mark >= 90 Then Return "A"
ElseIf mark >= 80 Then Return "B"
ElseIf mark >= 70 Then Return "C"
ElseIf mark >= 60 Then Return "D"
Else Return "F"
End If
End Function

